sol:'Stability of the energy landscape demands positive curvature in both directions: thermal ($C_V = T(\\partial S/\\partial T)_V \\gt 0$ — a warmed region must not suck more heat) and mechanical ($\\kappa_T \\gt 0$ — a squeezed region must push back). Violating either lets fluctuations run away into a phase split.',
