sol:'Count: $P(C-1) + 2$ free intensive variables (fractions per phase, plus $T$, $P$) minus $C(P-1)$ chemical-potential equalities between phases leaves $F = C - P + 2$. One component: triple point $F = 0$ (a point), two-phase line $F = 1$, single phase $F = 2$ — the phase diagram\'s skeleton law.',
